{"term":"recall","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:542716b763986e4c30","definition":"To withdraw, retract (one's words etc.); to revoke (an order).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["withcall","abjure","backpedal","disavow","disown","eat one's words","recall","recant","retract","revoke","swallow","take back","unsay","unspeak","walk back","withcall","withdraw"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["AFAIR","IIRC","misrecall","nonrecalled","recallability","recallable","recallee","recaller","recallism","recallist","recallment","unrecalled","YDNRC"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:730e6bb2f81870e572","definition":"To call back, bring back, or summon (someone) to a specific place, station, etc.","example":"He was recalled to service after his retirement.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["AFAIR","IIRC","misrecall","nonrecalled","recallability","recallable","recallee","recaller","recallism","recallist","recallment","unrecalled","YDNRC"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea239fba05ab633a40","definition":"To remove an elected official through a petition and direct vote.","example":"That stop-start-stop has created a groundswell of anger toward Mr. Newsom, a Democrat in the third year of his first term, that is increasingly fueling a movement to recall him from office in one of the bluest of blue states.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US","register":"US, transitive","wordFamily":["AFAIR","IIRC","misrecall","nonrecalled","recallability","recallable","recallee","recaller","recallism","recallist","recallment","unrecalled","YDNRC"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1994337ef83d0306ae","definition":"To bring back (someone) to or from a particular mental or physical state, activity etc.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["AFAIR","IIRC","misrecall","nonrecalled","recallability","recallable","recallee","recaller","recallism","recallist","recallment","unrecalled","YDNRC"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e840c2e9d9a0d0a7eb","definition":"To call back (a situation, event, etc.) to one's mind; to remember; to recollect.","example":"Nevertheless, there were many passengers on the recent special trains to whom the immaculate little 80-year-old \"Terrier,\" No. 32636, formerly Fenchurch, and its two L.B.S.C.R. coaches, recalled nostalgic memories of the old days on the line, when the trains were always spick and span; and days when the Kemp Town branch train was packed to capacity.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["AFAIR","IIRC","misrecall","nonrecalled","recallability","recallable","recallee","recaller","recallism","recallist","recallment","unrecalled","YDNRC"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:46c2becf432c31071d","definition":"To hearken back to, evoke; to be reminiscent of.","example":"\"The twinkling of the dancers' feet\" comes to us in the Odyssey as a memory from that palace of Alkinoos, whose wonders recall to us so much that we have fou